m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Glutamate\nOVERALL STRATEGY: Exploit a shared iron-mediated C4/C3 organic-acid lineage to converge on 2-oxoglutarate, the direct keto-acid precursor of glutamate. Succinate, fumarate, malate, oxaloacetate, or pyruvate can enter the network; oxaloacetate thermally decarboxylates to pyruvate, pyruvate couples with glyoxylate to form 2-oxoglutarate, and the amino group is installed either by H2-driven hydrothermal reductive amination on Fe-S minerals or by UV/ZnS photoreductive amination in shallow surface settings. Five entry points paired with two terminal amination modes yield ten connected pathways.\n\nMOLECULES (10 nodes):\n  - mol_001: C4H6O4 (succinate) [starting]\n  - mol_002: C4H4O4 (fumarate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_003: C4H6O5 (malate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_004: C4H4O5 (oxaloacetate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_005: C2H2O3 (glyoxylate) [starting]\n  - mol_006: C3H4O3 (pyruvate) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_007: C5H6O5 (alpha-ketoglutarate) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_009: H2 (hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_010: C5H9NO4 (glutamate) [target]\n\nREACTIONS (7 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_001 -> mol_002 (Succinate dehydrogenation to fumarate) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_002: mol_002 -> mol_003 (Fumarate hydration