m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Glutamate\nOVERALL STRATEGY: A single anoxic surface-geothermal setting is used throughout, so no hydrothermal-to-surface transfer step is needed. The network converges on alpha-ketoglutarate by two chemically distinct lineages: a C6 tricarboxylate lineage (citrate -> cis-aconitate -> isocitrate -> oxalosuccinate -> alpha-ketoglutarate) and a C2+C3 condensation lineage (pyruvate + glyoxylate -> 4-hydroxy-2-oxoglutarate -> 2-oxopent-3-enedioate -> alpha-ketoglutarate). Glutamate is then obtained by two explicit reductive amination chemistries, one H2-driven and one formate-driven. Ten pathways are generated by pairing five entry pools with these two terminal amination options, while keeping all redox and water bookkeeping explicit.\n\nMOLECULES (15 nodes):\n  - mol_001: H2 (hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_002: H2O (water) [starting]\n  - mol_003: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n  - mol_004: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_005: CH2O2 (formic acid) [starting]\n  - mol_006: C5H9NO4 (glutamate) [target]\n  - mol_007: C5H6O5 (alpha-ketoglutarate) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C3H4O3 (pyruvate) [starting]\n  - mol_009: C2H2O3 (glyoxylate) [starting]\n  - mol_010: C5H6O6 (4-hydroxy-2-oxoglutarate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_011: C5H4O5 (2-oxopent-3-enedioate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C6H8O7 (citrate) [starting]\n  - mol_013: C6H6O6 (cis-aconitate) [starting]\n  - mol_014: C6H8O7 (isocitrate) [starting]\n  - mol_015: C6H6O7 (oxalosuccinate) [starting]\n\nREACTIONS (9 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_012 -> mol_013, mol_002 (Citrate dehydration to cis-aconitate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_002: mol_013, mol_002 -> mol_014 (cis-Aconitate hydration to isocitrate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_003: mol_014 -> mol_015, mol_001 (Isocitrate dehydrogenation to oxalosuccinate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_015 -> mol_007, mol_003 (Oxalosuccinate decarboxylation to alpha-ketoglutarate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_005: mol_008, mol_009 -> mol_010 (Pyruvate-glyoxylate aldol addition to 4-hydroxy-2-oxoglutarate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_010 -> mol_011, mol_002 (4-Hydroxy-2-oxoglutarate dehydration to 2-oxopent-3-enedioate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_011, mol_001 -> mol_007 (2-Oxopent-3-enedioate hydrogenation to alpha-ketoglutarate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_007, mol_004, mol_001 -> mol_006, mol_002 (H2-driven reductive amination of alpha-ketoglutarate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_007, mol_004, mol_005 -> mol_006, mol_003, mol_002 (Formate-driven reductive amination of alpha-ketoglutarate) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Citrate route with H2 amination (5 steps)\n  - P2: Citrate route with formate amination (5 steps)\n  - P3: cis-Aconitate route with H2 amination (4 steps)\n  - P4: cis-Aconitate route with formate amination (4 steps)\n  - P5: Isocitrate route with H2 amination (3 steps)\n  - P6: Isocitrate route with formate amination (3 steps)\n  - P7: Oxalosuccinate route with H2 amination (2 steps)\n  - P8: Oxalosuccinate route with formate amination (2 steps)\n  - P9: Pyruvate-glyoxylate route with H2 amination (4 steps)\n  - P10: Pyruvate-glyoxylate route with formate amination (4 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions l